  "id": "behavioral-neuroscience",
  "term": "behavioral neuroscience",
  "definition": "Behavioral neuroscience is experimental research on behavior and related processes such as cognition and emotion, often using controlled tasks to examine mechanisms like learning and threat sensitivity. In translational work, it aims to connect laboratory findings with real-world maladaptive behavior and clinical conditions.",
